  "scope": "For a fixed disjoint-transpositions TF pair, the unconstrained labelled count is exactly 2^(choose(N-4,2)+2(N-4)+2), and the source-constrained fixed-pattern count is asymptotic to 2^(choose(N,2)-2N+3). For N>=16 the sharpened unlabelled lower bound is (19/20)2^(choose(N,2)-2N+3)/N!. In the full connected nonbipartite twin-free target class, L_n~3 choose(n,4)2^(choose(n-4,2)+2(n-4)+1), U_n~2^(choose(n-4,2)+2(n-4)-1)/(n-4)!, and U_n/g_n~2(n)_4/4^n. Almost all target graphs have Aut(G)=C2 and Aut(CDC(G))=D8 of order eight. Source: [Hujdurovic–Mitrovic, Problem 5.3, DOI 10.1002/jgt.23018](https://doi.org/10.1002/jgt.23018).",
  "status": "independently reviewed written mathematics; novelty unconfirmed; no all-parameter Lean",
  "integration_validation": "exact hashes, Python AST, JSON and dependency closure; no mathematical replay",
